# Forms: density, alignment, motion

- Lay out multi-field forms with `.form-grid` (12-col grid, defined in `globals.css`) and the per-field
  span classes: `field-xs` (zip/short codes), `field-sm` (phone/city/dates), `field-md` (name/email, half
  width), `field-lg`, `field-full` (address lines, textareas, submit row). Reuse these instead of
  hand-writing `grid-cols-*`/`col-span-*` so every form in the app aligns the same way.
- Every control in a form row (`Input`, `Select`, `Button`) shares one height via the `h-control` utility
  (backed by `--control-h` in `globals.css`), so a field and its adjacent button/icon-button line up.
  Don't override height ad hoc — change `--control-h` globally if the density needs to change.
- When content inside a form swaps (wizard step, tab panel, conditional field group), wrap it in
  `<AnimatedContent>` (`@/components/motion/animated-content`) keyed by the step/tab id, instead of a
  hard cut or `display:none` toggle. It crossfades and animates the height change so surrounding layout
  doesn't jump.
- Cards/panels containing a form get `shadow-sm` (or `shadow-md` if elevated/modal-like) plus the
  existing `border-border` — never a shadow without a border, never a heavy/dark drop shadow, never a
  custom inline `box-shadow`. The `shadow-xs/sm/md/lg` scale is already tuned in `globals.css`.
- Required/primary fields first, optional/secondary last. Label above input (not inline) for scanability
  in a dense grid.
